t was flying  I'd be like in rhythm fast taking off  [Music]  flock of birds I wouldn't even use  feathers I would probably use gloves for  that when it comes to eating  Marco might need to think about whether  the food is wet or dry or whether the  animal has a snout for example if it's a  horse  chewing celery I put my hands up to here  because you get a little bit of a a  cavity there and it's those cavities  that sell the sound on some occasions if  a digital library won't do he'll also  have to do the vocals himself  [Music]  to see a Foley artists thought process  about animal sounds in action  we put Marco to the test by showing him  a stock video clip with no sound that he  had never seen before definitely got a  few tracks to do cuz you got the claw on  the ground you got the claw on the thing  yet the teeth on the on the mat you got  the body movement the fur for the mat  Marco found one in his studio with very  similar material we do the the paws  first and for paws we just need a pair  of leather gloves for the lion's teeth  he used this small block of wood with  nails drilled into it which he created  for the tiger in Life of Pi work on sink  he brought back the wood blocks for the  Cubs scratching the claws which are very  similar to the teeth they have different  action they were pulling at it here it's  gripping I have the a few different  varieties of fur here we've got the the  astroturf the cat is moving along it so  we're gonna rub his body along the  bottom as he pulls himself forward real  close is a very small sound that'll be  the most convincing sound because all of  a sudden you go from just an animal  that's there moving around to you have  the feeling of it against the floor you  feel its its presence to top it all off  a few collar shakes and a few chews with  this little guy I'm only opening my  mouth and doing a like maybe 50% of the  volume I could get you know right now  he's got a little tongue lick that we're  gonna get up a little bit of a  slobbering sound remember cat also has a  dry tongue it might be a little  sandpapery but and you know what when  it's on itself it's just up then a fully  mixer watched the footage and layered it  all together  so what makes watching this without  sound and then with sound different the  sounds that we make brings you into the  personality of the animal you you become  closer to it and you want to give it a  personality you want to give the sounds  of personality and you can do it by its  sound movements  that's what fully artists do we give  detail  [Music]
 

